{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 3873464,
  "courseSlug": "nextjs-react-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Next.js & React - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "43341062",
      "title": "Configuring Dynamic Page Metadata",
      "lectureOrder": 203,
      "videoOrder": 189,
      "sourceHash": "a3d28d8a396edcbfc951e958ca45808f0ee882d3dd12da507f342fde966122ff",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.6,
          "end": 2.28,
          "en": "Now static metadata",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.28,
          "end": 4.74,
          "en": "as we have it here is often all you need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.74,
          "end": 6.54,
          "en": "because for many pages,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 6.54,
          "end": 10.53,
          "en": "the metadata you wanna set might indeed be static",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.53,
          "end": 14.073,
          "en": "and not change depending on what's shown on the page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.12,
          "end": 17.859,
          "en": "But you also might have some pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.859,
          "end": 20.97,
          "en": "where the metadata does change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.97,
          "end": 25.023,
          "en": "and does depend on the dynamic content of the page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.86,
          "end": 28.38,
          "en": "For example, here in my feed folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.38,
          "end": 32.67,
          "en": "in the page.js file there, I'm showing all my posts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.67,
          "end": 35.4,
          "en": "And of course we could set up some static metadata",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.4,
          "end": 39.68,
          "en": "here as well, with a title of All Posts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.68,
          "end": 44.58,
          "en": "and a description that could be, browse all our posts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.58,
          "end": 48.33,
          "en": "That might be fine and that might be all you need.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 48.33,
          "end": 52.149,
          "en": "But you also might have some dynamic metadata",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 52.149,
          "end": 56.73,
          "en": "on some pages, so some metadata that's not always the same,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 56.73,
          "end": 58.71,
          "en": "but that instead should change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 58.71,
          "end": 61.59,
          "en": "as the data on the page changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 61.59,
          "end": 64.92,
          "en": "For example, here, we might want a title that says,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.92,
          "end": 68.01,
          "en": "browse all our X posts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 68.01,
          "end": 70.86,
          "en": "where X should be the number of posts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 70.86,
          "end": 72.9,
          "en": "And of course that number is dynamic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 72.9,
          "end": 74.49,
          "en": "It's not set in stone",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.49,
          "end": 77.85,
          "en": "and we definitely don't know it at the point of time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 77.85,
          "end": 80.069,
          "en": "where we're writing this code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.069,
          "end": 83.051,
          "en": "And that's why NextJS also allows you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.051,
          "end": 85.621,
          "en": "to set dynamic metadata,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 85.621,
          "end": 90.621,
          "en": "and that's done by not exporting a constant called metadata,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 90.941,
          "end": 94.221,
          "en": "but by instead exporting a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 94.221,
          "end": 96.88,
          "en": "called generateMetadata.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 99.45,
          "end": 102.093,
          "en": "And that should be an async function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 103.77000000000001,
          "end": 106.5,
          "en": "And of course it must be named generateMetadata",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 106.5,
          "end": 109.11,
          "en": "because just as NextJS is looking",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 109.11,
          "end": 111.3,
          "en": "for a constant named metadata",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 111.3,
          "end": 113.07,
          "en": "or a variable that doesn't matter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 113.07,
          "end": 116.4,
          "en": "but it must be named metadata, NextJS is looking",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 116.4,
          "end": 119.75999999999999,
          "en": "for a function named generateMetadata like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 119.75999999999999,
          "end": 122.79,
          "en": "in your page.js files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 122.79,
          "end": 126.84,
          "en": "And if NextJS then finds such a exported function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 126.84,
          "end": 130.29,
          "en": "with that exact name, it will execute that function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 130.29,
          "end": 133.68,
          "en": "for you when it renders that page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 133.68,
          "end": 137.4,
          "en": "Now this function will then automatically receive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 137.4,
          "end": 140.61,
          "en": "a configuration object or a data object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 140.61,
          "end": 142.44,
          "en": "whatever you want to call it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 142.44,
          "end": 144.48,
          "en": "It will receive that object automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 144.48,
          "end": 146.7,
          "en": "because this object with its data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 146.7,
          "end": 149.07,
          "en": "will be passed in by NextJS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 149.07,
          "end": 152.37,
          "en": "And this object will hold useful information.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 152.37,
          "end": 156.549,
          "en": "For example, any page parameters that might be set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 156.549,
          "end": 160.82999999999998,
          "en": "for this page so that you could retrieve dynamic data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 160.82999999999998,
          "end": 163.59,
          "en": "if you were on a dynamic page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 163.59,
          "end": 166.65,
          "en": "But you can, for example, also extract any searchParams",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 166.65,
          "end": 169.011,
          "en": "that might be set in case these kinds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 169.011,
          "end": 172.35,
          "en": "of information pieces are important to you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 172.35,
          "end": 174.813,
          "en": "for generating the dynamic metadata.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 176.04,
          "end": 178.82999999999998,
          "en": "Now here for this page, I actually don't have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 178.82999999999998,
          "end": 181.05,
          "en": "any params or anything like that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 181.05,
          "end": 183.69,
          "en": "because I'm not on a dynamic route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 183.69,
          "end": 186.18,
          "en": "I don't have a dynamic route segment here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 186.18,
          "end": 188.76,
          "en": "Instead it's a regular static route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 188.76,
          "end": 191.52,
          "en": "but I still want dynamic metadata,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 191.52,
          "end": 195,
          "en": "therefore I'll still add generateMetadata,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 195,
          "end": 198.06,
          "en": "but I don't care about any data passed to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 198.06,
          "end": 201.693,
          "en": "But what I do care about is about my posts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 202.62,
          "end": 205.38,
          "en": "So here I will still get my posts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 205.38,
          "end": 207.903,
          "en": "by calling await getPosts here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 209.34,
          "end": 211.623,
          "en": "just as I do it in the page component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 212.79,
          "end": 215.52,
          "en": "So that here I get my posts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 215.52,
          "end": 219.011,
          "en": "and then I get my number of posts by using",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 219.011,
          "end": 222.813,
          "en": "or by accessing the length of this posts array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 223.95,
          "end": 228.18099999999998,
          "en": "And then once you're done preparing your dynamic data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 228.18099999999998,
          "end": 231.348,
          "en": "generateMetadata should return an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 231.348,
          "end": 235.29,
          "en": "where you then still set the title, description,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 235.29,
          "end": 238.74,
          "en": "and any other metadata you wanna set up.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 238.74,
          "end": 241.65,
          "en": "For example, we could still set a static description",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 241.65,
          "end": 245.883,
          "en": "of browse all our posts here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 246.87,
          "end": 250.71,
          "en": "but we could now also set a dynamic title that says,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 250.71,
          "end": 252.9,
          "en": "browse all our,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 252.9,
          "end": 257.9,
          "en": "and then the number of posts which I output here like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 260.21,
          "end": 263.763,
          "en": "since I'm using a string template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 265.2,
          "end": 269.22,
          "en": "And that's how we could dynamically generate such a metadata",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 269.22,
          "end": 273.093,
          "en": "object here with help of this generateMetadata function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 275.28,
          "end": 278.4,
          "en": "And that's really all that's to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 278.4,
          "end": 281.4,
          "en": "With that all, if I load this feed page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 281.4,
          "end": 286.23,
          "en": "it will generate as before, but NextJS will now actually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 286.23,
          "end": 290.15999999999997,
          "en": "also execute this generateMetadata function here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 290.15999999999997,
          "end": 292.77,
          "en": "and set the metadata accordingly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 292.77,
          "end": 295.35,
          "en": "That's why now after loading this page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 295.35,
          "end": 298.8,
          "en": "I see the number of posts here in the page title",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 298.8,
          "end": 302.583,
          "en": "because that metadata was generated dynamically.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
